widgets_values:
Illustrate this everyday moment, and nothing else: {{example_en}}

The headword is {{word}} ({{pos}} — {{sense_en}}); it is what the picture is about. Draw the same action, the same objects, the same number of people or things, the same place, and the same time of day the moment states. If it states a habitual or general truth rather than one event, depict the typical instance it implies, at the moment it puts itself in: morning sunlight must actually flood the room, rain must actually be falling, a weekly lunch must actually be laid on the table. Keep every element it names visible and recognisable, and add no people, animals, props, buildings, vehicles or weather it does not imply. Never swap the moment for a metaphor, a symbol, a mood board or a collage.

Art direction: mid-century modern editorial illustration, like a plate from a vintage illustrated field guide. Limited palette of deep ink navy, warm terracotta, mustard ochre, muted sage green and soft sky blue on warm cream paper. Flat geometric shapes, confident clean silhouettes, subtle risograph grain and paper texture, gentle shading, generous negative space, centered square composition, calm and charming mood, one clear focal group or a readable action with every participant visible, textless.

